    <title>Japan Travel Handbook</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; padding: 20px; }
        h1, h2 { color: #333; }
        .section { margin-bottom: 20px; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Japan Travel Handbook</h1>
    
    <div class="section">
        <h2>Itinerary</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Monday, April 15: Tokyo</li>
            <li>Tuesday, April 16: Tokyo</li>
            <li>Wednesday, April 17: Tokyo</li>
            <li>Thursday, April 18: Kyoto</li>
            <li>Friday, April 19: Kyoto</li>
            <li>Saturday, April 20: Kyoto</li>
            <li>Sunday, April 21: Nara</li>
            <li>Monday, April 22: Osaka</li>
            <li>Tuesday, April 23: Osaka</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="section">
        <h2>Essential Japanese Phrases</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Hello: Konnichiwa (こんにちは)</li>
            <li>Thank you: Arigatou gozaimasu (ありがとうございます)</li>
            <li>Excuse me: Sumimasen (すみません)</li>
            <li>Where is...?: ... wa doko desu ka? (〜はどこですか？)</li>
            <li>How much?: Ikura desu ka? (いくらですか？)</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="section">
        <h2>Travel Tips</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Always carry cash, as many places don't accept credit cards</li>
            <li>Get a Japan Rail Pass for convenient and cost-effective travel</li>
            <li>Be respectful in temples and shrines</li>
            <li>Try onsen (hot springs) for a relaxing experience</li>
            <li>Use convenience stores for quick meals and ATMs</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</body>
</html>